1
00:02:24,759 --> 00:02:25,319
All done.

2
00:02:25,719 --> 00:02:26,400
You can move now.

3
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,719
You can move now.

4
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:35,599
You drew this so well.

5
00:02:46,199 --> 00:02:48,120
I want to name this piece.

6
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,039
What do you want to call it?

7
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:53,319
Angel.

8
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:55,840
What's that supposed to mean?

9
00:02:59,000 --> 00:02:59,719
Angel.

10
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:07,919
Do you like it?

11
00:03:10,759 --> 00:03:11,960
You're really bold.

12
00:03:13,039 --> 00:03:14,919
Didn't the brewery call for new beer labels?

13
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,159
So I submitted a design.

14
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:18,080
Never expected it'd actually get picked.

15
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,919
I sent it in anonymously.

16
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,960
No one knows I drew it.

17
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,319
And no one knows it's you.

18
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:31,039
Don't come around here anymore.

19
00:03:31,719 --> 00:03:32,680
During work hours,

20
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,919
outsiders aren't allowed in the workshop.

21
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:34,960
Now get going.

22
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,360
Let me ask you something.

23
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:51,960
What's this?

24
00:03:54,439 --> 00:03:55,360
Nothing.

25
00:03:55,759 --> 00:03:57,000
Just doodling.

26
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:58,080
Doodling?

27
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:58,800
Who did you draw?

28
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,319
None of your business.

29
00:04:02,639 --> 00:04:03,319
Tell me.

30
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,080
Who did you draw?

31
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,360
Answer me!

32
00:04:06,479 --> 00:04:07,159
What are you doing?

33
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:07,879
Sit down!

34
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,479
Did you draw Liu Xuemei?

35
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:13,360
You think I'm blind?

36
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,199
Like I can't tell?

37
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:19,279
Are you seeing her?

38
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:25,800
Fine.

39
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:26,759
Fine.

40
00:04:27,519 --> 00:04:28,639
I'm not gonna argue with you.

41
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,959
Let's talk this through calmly.

42
00:04:33,759 --> 00:04:34,439
I'm your father.

43
00:04:34,439 --> 00:04:34,959
Right?

44
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,800
I wouldn't steer you wrong, would I?

45
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,879
At your age,

46
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:41,399
dating someone

47
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,480
is completely normal.

48
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,480
But whoever you're with,

49
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,600
it can't be a divorced woman in her thirties

50
00:04:46,639 --> 00:04:49,160
who already has a kid!

51
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,959
This Liu Xuemei...

52
00:04:52,079 --> 00:04:53,519
What... what does she even do?

53
00:04:53,759 --> 00:04:55,160
A Beer Taster.

54
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,360
And what about you?

55
00:04:56,639 --> 00:04:58,759
A college graduate!

56
00:04:58,879 --> 00:05:01,160
How did you get mixed up with her?

57
00:05:01,519 --> 00:05:02,600
You like her?

58
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,839
What's so great about her?

59
00:05:05,319 --> 00:05:06,839
So what if I like her?

60
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,920
Say that again!

61
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,160
What century are we in?

62
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,959
You even want to police my love life?

63
00:05:12,439 --> 00:05:13,439
You're so annoying!

64
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,120
Get back here!

65
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,279
Xuemei!

66
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:41,800
Chen Yuan.

67
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,480
We shouldn't see each other anymore.

68
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:47,160
Why?

69
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,800
Chief Engineer Chen has known for a while.

70
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,480
I could tell.

71
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,519
Your dad is an educated man.

72
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,480
He cares about his dignity.

73
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,839
Something like this...

74
00:05:58,399 --> 00:05:59,759
he could never tell anyone.

75
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,759
He's him, and I'm me.

76
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,680
I don't care what he thinks.

77
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,399
Don't talk out of spite.

78
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,920
You two are family.

79
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,600
He wouldn't steer you wrong.

80
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,800
You should listen to him.

81
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,040
Xuemei.

82
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,839
I don't want to break up with you.

83
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,800
Listen to me.

84
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,199
Go home and get a good night's sleep.

85
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,839
Just treat our time together...

86
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,279
as a dream.

87
00:06:34,199 --> 00:06:34,839
Goodbye.

88
00:06:36,519 --> 00:06:37,399
Xuemei, don't go!

89
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,319
I really can't live without you.

90
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,560
I want to be with you for the rest of my life, Xuemei.

91
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,120
Please.

92
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,639
Don't give up on me, okay?

93
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,279
This is my dorm's number.

94
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,279
You'll call me,

95
00:06:52,439 --> 00:06:53,040
right?

96
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:08,800
Chen Yuan.

97
00:07:09,079 --> 00:07:10,040
Phone for you.

98
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:14,279
Xuemei.

99
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,600
How've you been lately?

100
00:07:16,439 --> 00:07:17,279
I'm doing great.

101
00:07:21,199 --> 00:07:22,879
Just that I can't see you.

102
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:24,319
I miss you so much.

103
00:07:25,519 --> 00:07:26,560
I'm in Qingzhou.

104
00:07:28,439 --> 00:07:29,000
Really?

105
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:29,839
Meet at the usual spot.

106
00:07:29,879 --> 00:07:30,519
Wait for me.

107
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:31,360
Wait for me, okay?

108
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,279
Thank you, Auntie.

109
00:07:49,519 --> 00:07:50,160
Xuemei.

110
00:07:55,639 --> 00:07:56,480
You must be cold.

111
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:39,720
Hurry up and go.

112
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,240
Auntie,

113
00:08:45,279 --> 00:08:46,720
did anyone call Chen Yuan?

114
00:08:46,759 --> 00:08:47,320
Yeah.

115
00:08:47,919 --> 00:08:48,840
They called quite a few times.

116
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:49,480
When?

117
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:50,519
About an hour ago.

118
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:52,279
The phone.

119
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,840
Your hands are freezing.

120
00:10:03,399 --> 00:10:04,879
Come on,

121
00:10:04,879 --> 00:10:07,039
I'll take you out for hot pot.

122
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,320
We'll celebrate the new millennium together.

123
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,320
Happy New Year!

124
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,240
Happy New Year!

125
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,240
Of course I want to go with you,

126
00:10:15,399 --> 00:10:16,840
but I promised my coworkers

127
00:10:17,039 --> 00:10:18,120
I'd go to the auction with them.

128
00:10:18,799 --> 00:10:20,440
But tonight is Millennium Eve!

129
00:10:20,799 --> 00:10:22,320
It only happens once every thousand years.

130
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:24,200
Over there,

131
00:10:24,919 --> 00:10:25,919
they have so many people.

132
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:27,720
Here, I only have you.

133
00:10:28,679 --> 00:10:29,720
After today,

134
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,720
the brewery will belong to all of us.

135
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,720
This excitement...

136
00:10:34,039 --> 00:10:35,000
Can you feel it?

137
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:38,080
I just want to be with you.

138
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,559
All right, Mr. Chen.

139
00:10:41,879 --> 00:10:42,480
Be good.

140
00:10:42,799 --> 00:10:43,360
I promise you,

141
00:10:43,679 --> 00:10:45,720
I'll call you right on time tonight.

142
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:47,679
We'll ring in the new year over the phone.

143
00:10:48,159 --> 00:10:48,639
Five,

144
00:10:49,159 --> 00:10:49,679
four,

145
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,519
three,

146
00:10:51,039 --> 00:10:51,559
two,

147
00:10:51,879 --> 00:10:52,399
one.

148
00:10:52,559 --> 00:10:54,960
Happy New Year!

149
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,360
All right.

150
00:10:56,399 --> 00:10:56,840
I'm running late.

151
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:57,399
I've got to go.

152
00:11:00,399 --> 00:11:01,279
I'll be waiting!

153
00:11:03,159 --> 00:11:03,960
Midnight sharp!

154
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:09,360
She must've been waiting for my call the whole time.

155
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:14,799
We promised to ring in the millennium together,

156
00:11:16,679 --> 00:11:17,919
counting down together.

157
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,080
I'm so sorry.

158
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:35,639
So, according to your story,

159
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:37,000
you stole the videotapes

160
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,039
just to see Liu Xuemei again.

161
00:11:41,399 --> 00:11:42,080
Yes.

162
00:11:43,399 --> 00:11:45,240
Because Xuemei was a Beer Taster.

163
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:48,159
The biggest taboo for a Beer Taster is drinking.

164
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,960
To keep her palate sensitive,

165
00:11:51,159 --> 00:11:52,679
she never drank.

166
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,720
So how could she have possibly drunk to excess?

167
00:11:57,559 --> 00:11:59,759
I found it suspicious right from the start.

168
00:12:00,759 --> 00:12:01,759
Only back then,

169
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,480
I was afraid of everything,

170
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:06,960
so I never dared to ask.

171
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,320
So you believe Liu Xuemei

172
00:12:10,679 --> 00:12:11,600
died of unnatural causes?

173
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,799
I don't believe she would drink that much.

174
00:12:14,879 --> 00:12:16,679
A woman who never touched a drop...

175
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,200
How could she freeze to death while drunk?

176
00:12:21,879 --> 00:12:23,720
I don't believe she drank all that alcohol!

177
00:12:24,159 --> 00:12:24,879
It's impossible!

178
00:12:29,879 --> 00:12:31,279
Someone was trying to kill her.

179
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:36,559
Weren't they?

180
00:12:47,399 --> 00:12:49,279
Do you know who the traitor was back then?

181
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:54,600
All I know is

182
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,120
they said Xuemei was the traitor.

183
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,320
I don't believe that.

184
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:04,759
As for anything else,

185
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:06,440
I have no idea.

186
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:10,600
Then can you tell us

187
00:13:10,679 --> 00:13:12,879
why you erased what was on the tape?

188
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,840
It really was an accident.

189
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,600
I already explained this to Shen Leshui.

190
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:19,600
It's just that

191
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:21,399
I hadn't used an old machine like that in so long.

192
00:13:22,559 --> 00:13:23,720
I can pay her for it.

193
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:27,039
Do you have any recollection

194
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,480
of what the content you erased

195
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,120
actually was?

196
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:35,960
I don't know.

197
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:48,960
How did it go?

198
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:50,279
For all three murders,

199
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:51,639
he has alibis.

200
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,399
Then why did he erase my tapes?

201
00:13:58,039 --> 00:13:59,320
He said it was an accident.

202
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:02,360
Besides, there's no evidence it was deliberate.

203
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:05,840
It was purely out of guilt toward Liu Xuemei

204
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:07,320
that he stole your tapes.

205
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:10,639
He confessed everything.

206
00:14:11,679 --> 00:14:12,639
He was pretty cooperative.

207
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,679
You must've done a lot of persuading.

208
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:15,440
Thanks for your hard work.

209
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:19,919
Here's the letter of forgiveness.

210
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:22,200
I don't plan to press charges.

211
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,879
After all,

212
00:14:24,519 --> 00:14:25,720
he's my friend's husband,

213
00:14:26,559 --> 00:14:27,440
Xiaohu's father.

214
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:34,519
Then...

215
00:14:34,519 --> 00:14:35,879
the erased footage,

216
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:37,360
can it be recovered?

217
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:44,200
Let's check the tapes at your place later.

218
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,000
Sure.

219
00:14:53,919 --> 00:14:54,879
Why did you

220
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:56,919
steal Shen Leshui's tapes?

221
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,559
It's because of Liu Xuemei, isn't it?

222
00:15:09,399 --> 00:15:11,440
I really see you in a whole new light.

223
00:15:15,639 --> 00:15:17,399
Turns out your lack of romance

224
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:21,159
depends on the person.

225
00:15:26,039 --> 00:15:26,919
I'm sorry.

226
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,440
When we first got married,

227
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:04,000
I always felt

228
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,799
your heart wasn't in it.

229
00:16:07,679 --> 00:16:08,720
But you were

230
00:16:09,919 --> 00:16:10,679
good to me,

231
00:16:12,559 --> 00:16:13,399
really sincere,

232
00:16:15,639 --> 00:16:16,519
and hardworking.

233
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,120
Didn't you always say

234
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,159
that's just life,

235
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,120
that's how it is?

236
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:27,440
So I thought

237
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:32,600
we had our whole lives ahead of us,

238
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:38,159
and things would only get better.

239
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,399
But I never expected this.

240
00:16:47,159 --> 00:16:47,879
I'm sorry.

241
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,480
I shouldn't have kept it from you.

242
00:16:57,159 --> 00:16:59,399
I just didn't want to reopen that wound.

243
00:17:03,519 --> 00:17:05,279
I wanted to take this secret

244
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,799
to my grave.

245
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:12,799
I just never thought that after all these years,

246
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:17,119
it would be dragged back out.

247
00:17:23,079 --> 00:17:24,359
You sure know how to keep things bottled up,

248
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:26,480
Chen Yuan.

249
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:35,759
The house, the car...

250
00:17:37,079 --> 00:17:38,039
they're all in your name.

251
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,319
If...

252
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,400
if you want a divorce,

253
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,680
I'll walk away with nothing.

254
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:09,960
Xiaohu is still young.

255
00:18:12,119 --> 00:18:13,480
I don't want him to think

256
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:15,880
his dad was this or that.

257
00:18:29,559 --> 00:18:31,000
We're going to my dad's for dinner next week.

258
00:18:32,559 --> 00:18:33,680
Go buy a couple bottles of liquor.

259
00:18:52,559 --> 00:18:54,759
I... I only have 500 yuan on me right now.

260
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:55,799
Um...

261
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,799
I'll... I'll give you

262
00:18:57,799 --> 00:18:58,319
this much for now,

263
00:18:58,599 --> 00:18:59,720
and go back to get the rest.

264
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,440
Which tape was erased?

265
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:10,799
This one.

266
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,240
That was the day of the auction.

267
00:19:20,119 --> 00:19:22,039
Ma Guowen didn't want the workers at the auction,

268
00:19:22,599 --> 00:19:24,240
so he locked them inside the factory.

269
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,160
Everything after this is gone, right?

270
00:19:33,599 --> 00:19:34,000
Yeah.

271
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,839
If he erased the shots of Liu Xuemei,

272
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:37,920
I could understand that.

273
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,440
But she isn't on this tape.

274
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,599
Besides, on the day of the auction,

275
00:19:43,759 --> 00:19:45,640
she was with him in Qingzhou.

276
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,799
He knew that.

277
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,559
There's a date on the tape, too.

278
00:19:49,519 --> 00:19:51,480
So why would he erase a tape

279
00:19:51,559 --> 00:19:53,279
that had nothing to do with him?

280
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,519
I think

281
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,160
Chen Yuan isn't that simple.

282
00:19:58,519 --> 00:19:59,680
He must be hiding something.

283
00:20:04,759 --> 00:20:06,559
This shot looks kind of familiar to me.

284
00:20:06,599 --> 00:20:07,480
Wasn't this in your

285
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:08,480
final cut of Malt Kingdom?

286
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,160
Did it appear? 'Go to the venue!'

287
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,440
That's impossible.

288
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:12,279
Back then, the TV station cut all

289
00:20:12,279 --> 00:20:14,880
the footage about buying the factory.

290
00:20:15,559 --> 00:20:16,160
Really?

291
00:20:18,799 --> 00:20:19,400
'Go to the venue!'

292
00:20:19,759 --> 00:20:20,359
'Go to the venue!'

293
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,160
Wait a second.

294
00:20:35,319 --> 00:20:35,680
Hold it.

295
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:36,880
Right in this corner.

296
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,400
Isn't that the exact same?

297
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,039
Right?

298
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,759
They couldn't find good shots of smiling faces then,

299
00:20:50,279 --> 00:20:51,720
so they used this footage from the factory shutdown.

300
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,240
Pretty slick editing.

301
00:20:53,559 --> 00:20:54,880
The audience was completely fooled.

302
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,000
You can't tell at all

303
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,559
how tense things actually were back then.

304
00:20:58,119 --> 00:21:00,440
Twisting the truth is really that simple.

305
00:21:01,359 --> 00:21:02,680
Different editing techniques,

306
00:21:02,759 --> 00:21:03,839
set to different music,

307
00:21:04,039 --> 00:21:04,920
to build an atmosphere,

308
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,279
and the audience gets fooled.

309
00:21:09,279 --> 00:21:10,559
Just like on my video channel.

310
00:21:10,559 --> 00:21:11,200
Is that so?

311
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,440
Sorry about that.

312
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:18,039
Then I don't get it.

313
00:21:18,079 --> 00:21:20,039
Why did Chen Yuan want to erase this part?

314
00:21:34,599 --> 00:21:36,319
Is that Chen Qingchun in the distance?

315
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:38,160
What's he holding in his hand?

316
00:21:43,079 --> 00:21:44,359
Looks like a key ring.

317
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:46,400
That guy handed Chen Qingchun a key ring.

318
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:50,720
That guy's from Security.

319
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:55,440
That makes him Ma Guowen's man.

320
00:21:58,519 --> 00:22:01,559
So Chen Yuan didn't want anyone to know

321
00:22:02,079 --> 00:22:03,119
that back then, his father

322
00:22:03,119 --> 00:22:05,039
was already colluding with Ma Guowen.

323
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,079
Whoa there!

324
00:22:47,079 --> 00:22:48,519
Easy, brother!

325
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:49,559
Slow down, take it easy.

326
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:50,599
Careful now.

327
00:22:52,319 --> 00:22:52,799
Take it easy.

328
00:22:52,799 --> 00:22:53,799
Almost took a tumble there.

329
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:54,640
You okay?

330
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,079
Have a seat right here. Okay.

331
00:22:56,079 --> 00:22:56,640
Alright, alright, thanks.

332
00:22:57,039 --> 00:22:57,960
I'll set this over there for you.

333
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:58,519
I got it, I got it.

334
00:22:58,839 --> 00:22:59,480
You're a good kid.

335
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:00,039
Waitress!

336
00:23:01,519 --> 00:23:02,359
Anyone else,

337
00:23:02,759 --> 00:23:03,599
